statement:
Let $k$ be a field, $X$ a scheme proper over $k$ [def-weil-proper-morphism] and $\mathcal F$ a coherent $\mathcal O_X$-module [pqf-def-coherent] whose support $\operatorname{Supp}(\mathcal F)=\{x\in X:\mathcal F_x
e0\}$ has dimension $\le0$ [def-kun-topological-krull-dimension]. Then, with the cohomology $H^i(X,-)$ and Euler characteristic $\chi(X,-)$ of [def-pc-euler-characteristic]:

1. $H^i(X,\mathcal F)=0$ for all $i>0$;
1. $\chi(X,\mathcal F)=\dim_kH^0(X,\mathcal F)=\dim_k\Gamma(X,\mathcal F)$;
1. for every invertible $\mathcal O_X$-module $\mathcal N$ [def-sc-invertible-module] the module $\mathcal F\otimes_{\mathcal O_X}\mathcal N$ is coherent with the same support, and $\chi(X,\mathcal F\otimes_{\mathcal O_X}\mathcal N)=\chi(X,\mathcal F)$.
